83 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 276 0 R
/E (Memory is a vital function that helps us process information, make decisions, and learn effectively. It is a primary function we use everyday, and being able to understand and enhance it can reap massive benefits.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 277 0 R
/E (Memory consists of three main steps: encoding, retention, retrieval. Each of these tasks are distinct from each other and are essential for processing and storing information in the brain. Consequently, any malfunction in these processes can result in difficulty performing simple tasks and induce stress and frustration in individuals. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 278 0 R
/E (Metacognitive awareness is the ability to identify when the brain is focused and which areas perform the best during specific tasks. This is essential in forming memories as it allows individuals to recognize how they perform best, and utilize those strengths to their benefit. Hence, it can also help identify degradation in memory, and achieve early intervention to prevent the progression of any memory problems. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 279 0 R
/E (The Muse 2 is an EEG headset with advanced technology, making it an excellent tool to achieve metacognitive awareness for an affordable price.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 280 0 R
/E (In this project, I used the Muse 2 headset to create an accessible and affordable program which helps individuals achieve metacognitive awareness.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (Around the world, over 55 million individuals suffer from dementia, with 60-70% of that population experiencing Alzheimer's. Around a quarter of the population on the planet experience memory problems such as brain fog and other types of forgetfulness. These types of problems can cause difficulty in performing basic tasks, and can lead to frustration and stress. Most of the time, people cannot identify and get these problems diagnosed because of accessibility struggles and issues with EEG procedures in the lab. These reasons are listed below:)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 281 0 R
/E (The cost for lab EEGs can exceed $5,000 per day for certain tests, which is one reason people might feel that a few forgetful instances is not worth getting checked, as the majority of people do not have access to this kind of money.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 282 0 R
/E (The wait times for EEG tests are extremely long, as many many hospitals do not have access to many EEG systems. Even after the test is done, it can take weeks for the participant to receive their results, which can lead to any underlying conditions worsening over that periods of time.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 283 0 R
/E (During the test, many participants with thick, curly, or braided hair might be asked to cut or remove their hair, which is a main reason why many people might not want to participate in a EEG test, as some people naturally have hair that might not be able to work with an EEG.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 284 0 R
/E (Hospitals and academic institutions which have EEGs might be far away or inaccessible for many people, especially those living in poor or rural areas. The process for applying and receiving EEG tests is long and complicated, taking a long time for application and selection. This might discourage many to not take these tests because of the inaccessibility.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 285 0 R
/E (The test itself could take many hours and can be tedious and uncomfortable for many, and the stress of a lab environment might affect the results from the test, potentially leading to false results and misdiagnosis and treatment, which can worsen the problem, or cause healthy individuals to receive incorrect and possibly dangerous treatment.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (My project aims to fix these problems and provide a cheap, fast, and low pressure test which can give participants accurate results and highlight their strengths and weaknesses in memory. It will make memory testing much more accessible and efficient to people who have low income and live in rural or poor areas.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (It will also be able to provides strengths which individuals can utilize to further expand their memory and use techniques which will help them succeed academically and beyond in life.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
