98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 286 0 R
/E (The first limitation is that the Muse 2 headset does not possess the same capability as a proper EEG cap, or EEGs used in labs. Though it has very reliable data, the limitation of the area of the electrodes makes some of the brainwaves not entirely accurate, as the headset is initally designed for relaxation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (Also, though there is filteration, some signals from eyes and muscle movements can affect the data, as well as oil and hair between the electrodes can weaken the connection. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 288 0 R
/E (The Bluetooth connection between the headset and the laptop may falter at times, providing incorrect time for some of the events.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (The participant may also has external factors influencing them, potentially determining how they do on the game, and whether the brainwaves that are recorded are accurate to how their brain works. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E (The project also does not measure long-term memory, which is very significant, and it the program does not test for long periods of time. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
