>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 308 0 R
/E (The filtration process consists of many steps to ensure that the data is accurate and removes any unnecessary components from the files. It uses mne-python to access EEG filters. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 309 0 R
/E (The first step is to apply a bandpass filter to the data. This filter is set for 1-40 Hz, and this ensures that the data is purely the participants brainwaves, as the highest brainwaves only goes up to 40 Hz. It removes extra waves from muscles and eyes, )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 310 0 R
/E (The second step is to compute an average reference from all of the brainwaves, as the natural setting can be to reference all the data from the two frontal sensors. This makes sure that all the data is computed equally from all four electrodes, retaining accuracy for the report. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 311 0 R
/E (The third step is to use ICA \(Independent Component Analysis\) to further filter out artifacts such as eye and muscles movement more precisely and accurately. This analyzes the data and finds more specific instances of eye and muscle artifacts and removes them from the data. This ensures accuracy in the results. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 312 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (The last step is to extract the engagement and focus use the theta and beta brainwaves and using them to generate the final report. They are organized to determine in which games the participant was most engaged and focused in, and achieve metacognitive awareness. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 81 0 R
/T (Recording & Saving)
/E (Recording & Saving)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 314 0 R
/E (In order to stream data from the Muse 2 headset to the laptop, I had to use a third-party software called Brainflow. This software uses a BLE \(Bluetooth Low Energy\) system to connect with the headset. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 315 0 R
/E (Brainflow will take data from the 4 electrodes on the headset and stream them to the laptop so that the data is ordered properly and accurately received from all 4 electrodes. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 316 0 R
/E (While the user is playing the memory games, Unity is sending the Python app timestamps for the beginning and ending of each game. The timestamps are sent through UDP \(User Datagram Protocol\) markers, which are extremely precise and ultra fast, ensuring that the data is transmitted accurately. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 317 0 R
/E (After, the EEG data is organized into a FIF file, ensuring all the data from the four electrodes is retained. The UDP timestamps are organized into a CSV file, which are then used with the FIF files to ensure that the data is orientated properly with the beginning and end of the games. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 318 0 R
/E (The data is now saved and ready to be processed and filtered to generate the report. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
